docs/DECISIONS.md:2329:## D167 · 2026-10-25 · No hard-coded identity for aggregates; the judge gets the evidence, the vocabulary gets the missing measures, the writer owns replacement
docs/DECISIONS.md:2334:- The writer owns the replacement rule (06-views, the Replace row): a piece may replace one in force only with a stated day not earlier than the stored one's, a tier at least the stored one's (fact and party statement above third-party view above rumour), and, between two third-party views, the same party; otherwise it is stored as new. Found when Jev's `supersedes` let analysts' reactions retire reported facts (log rows 39–41); the rule applies to both matching engines.
docs/DECISIONS.md:2340:- **A repeat may name the piece shown for the same evidence under another of its theses** (`matching.check`). 06-views step 6: a repeat adds a source and any new thesis link; the writer already resolves a piece to one stored identity for all its theses. The check required the target under the destination thesis and failed an item twice (9 of 17 such refusals over four ledgers were this case). A replacement still stays within its thesis.
docs/DECISIONS.md:2341:- **The Jev replace criterion carries the PRD's full definition**: a later version of the same statement or number, changed (the same speaker revises it, an official confirms or denies that claim, the original source revises it); another statement on the same topic is not this (06-views lines 191, 197, 306). Probed against a fresh control, three samples: wrong replacements 10 of 10 removed on the seed and week, 6 of 7 out of sample on August; the right ones that stay are the guidance revisions and a source revising its own figure. A second wording ('the same party') was rejected by its pre-registered rule.
docs/DECISIONS.md:2342:- **The writer's replacement rule, generalised from the PRD**: an incoming third-party view or rumour replaces only the same party's earlier piece (subsumes the view-over-view rule of D167). On every stored ledger it refuses 6 written replacements, all a commentator's view over another party's rumour, none right.
docs/DECISIONS.md:2591:- Measured ([results](research/2026-10-27-stage34-gold/results.md), 2026-10-27 23:05–23:30, $0.24): the 24-case gold was written, then re-read as a hedge-fund analyst's standard (eight rules in `gold.md`, Alex: "做一个 hedge fund analyst 的专业视角去看怎么做这一步的标准"). One send per case of the new path (step 2 reader → Jev opinions → one gpt-6-luna call with the complete context): step 4 places and merges right on 20 of 21 development and 3 of 3 held-out cases, never retires a different statement; two misses (G09 the denial not written into the argument, G11 a bank's echo taken as independent). Jev's piece opinions are right on 7 of 18; the product's replace class has its mechanism in the `supersedes` criterion ("an official confirms or denies that reported claim"): re-sending the 47 stored replacements, 16 do not reproduce and 7 flip to a `contradicts` class once the clause is split out. Two harness contradictions of the assistant's (a check refusing what the prompt asked; the record's own id) were fixed at $0, and nine gold rows were corrected from verified ledger ids (the gold had been written from a ranked excerpt, not the complete expansion). No production change yet: the writer still acts on Jev's label.
docs/DECISIONS.md:2593:## D202 · 2026-10-27 · The writer retires nothing on a matching label: a replacement is recorded as a revision and both pieces stay in force
docs/DECISIONS.md:2595:- Alex, on the arm1 result and the proposal: "你接着做，需要非常严谨的看结果和测量". Census first ([labels](research/2026-10-27-stage34-gold/replacements-47-labels.json), every pair read): of the run's 47 retirements, 22 are the owner's later value or status of the same claim (right under rule E), 20 retired a statement that should have stayed (10 a contradiction or qualification, among them a denial erasing the delay report, "subject to final agreements" erasing the $500bn announcement; 10 a different matter), 5 were restatements mislabelled. Jev's `supersedes` label does not separate them: 17 of 22 right and 12 of 20 wrong carry it; with "confirms or denies" split out (`jev_contradicts.py`) 4 wrong ones flip to `contradicts` but so do 3 right ones. No label the matcher gives is safe to retire on.
docs/DECISIONS.md:2596:- Decided: `writing` no longer calls `store.replace`. A `replace` decision stores the incoming piece, links it wherever the target is linked, and records the pair in a new `revisions` table (old, new, said day, seq); both pieces stay in force. `replacement_refused` becomes `revision_refused` with the same conditions (a stated day, a tier at least the old piece's, the same party for views and rumours): refused means stored as new without the relation, as before. The late-older-statement rule is unchanged. `replacements` is history: read by every present reader as before, never written again. `store.evidence_in_force` carries `revises` (the predecessor by revision) and judging prints "It revises eX (both in force)" so the judge sees the path; the library UI and service do not show revisions yet (open). The Jev criteria are unchanged: the split was measured and not adopted (3 false `contradicts` on right revisions against 4 catches).
docs/DECISIONS.md:2599:- Regression week ([results](research/2026-10-27-stage34-gold/results.md), `english-v34b-nvda-week-2026-10-27`, $0.23, 98 items, none failed): the whole path runs with the revision rule; `replacements` gains no row. Counts differ from the v18 week (129 against 176 evidence rows, 12 against 9 theses) because extraction is a sampler, not because of the writer; the writer's effect is proved on the decisions themselves. Reading the week's one `replace` decision found a second silent loss in the same code path: an incoming statement said before its target was logged in `late_statements` and linked nowhere (both weeks dropped SemiAnalysis's Kyber delay report this way; the three-month run dropped the SharonAI backstop figure; 1 of 3,216 decisions, each a material statement). Fixed in the same slice: an older statement is stored and linked as one more piece, no revision recorded, the log row kept. Test red on the old writer, green after; suite 209. Observed, not fixed here: 34 of 1,530 stored pieces carry a non-ISO `original_day` ("2026-07-05 to 2026-07-06", "2026-03"), which is what made the Kyber report "older"; an extraction-contract item for the next pass.
docs/DECISIONS.md:2630:## D207 · 2026-10-28 · Statements are filed by a separate placement call under the one-home rule; an unfiled statement is kept (extraction v20, `poc-v36`)
docs/DECISIONS.md:2632:- Alex, on the root cause ("你还是没有根因的去解决这个问题 … 要么挂不到，要么挂多"; "跑那个归档实验"; "你看着结果来做"; "一样的标准开始测"). The mechanism ([routing-analysis.md](research/2026-10-28-extraction-quality/routing-analysis.md)): the in-call link decision was a coin flip (36% right on the gold, 46–78 pieces kept from the same bytes) and the gate at once (an unlinked statement was dropped: 60% of all statements, ~15–30% of them material); the link rule routed demand news to the company-wide quantities (six root theses held 66% of all links; v2's pieces 86% double-linked, 26% cited); the thesis list had no driver layer.
docs/DECISIONS.md:2633:- Decided, three parts measured one at a time on the frozen gold (three draws each, 8 threads, $0.04–0.05 an arm) and on the first week's 255 in-call pieces: (1) `placement.py`: one call per item with the title line, the statements and the open questions, each with a code-written 'takes' line (key, event type, research-group names; aggregates admit other populations); the sift keeps statements without a link (`keep_unlinked`); the placer's links replace the extraction's, candidate links survive; a statement filed nowhere is stored in `unplaced_statements` with the handover. (2) The rule is the placement prompt: `placement-narrow-v1` — one home, the narrowest question; company-wide figure questions take only their own figures, guidance and management statements. (3) D42's "evidence is linked at extraction" becomes: the extraction's links are its first opinion; placement decides. Gated on the prompt version (`PLACEMENT_FROM = 20`); `cfg.placement` is required from v20.
docs/DECISIONS.md:2634:- Measured: core statements filed right 6/6/5 → 9/9/9 (with six seeded driver questions shown) and 9/10/9 under the old rule; wrong links 9 → 3; links to the two sinks 63/60/44 → 6/1/5; junk placed 53/48/32 → 39/27/35; every decisive matter statement (the Kyber/Rubin Ultra rack delay cluster, the AI Compute Partnership participants, Goldman's capex estimate) placed; one week through the whole path (`english-v36-nvda-1w-2026-10-28`, $0.22 against $0.22) kept 580 statements the old path dropped. Arms retired by measurement: the extraction's links shown as a hint (junk and sink links returned), group aliases alone (the groups lack the press names). Tests `tests/test_placement.py`, suite 222.
docs/DECISIONS.md:2635:- Not built here: re-placement of unplaced statements when a thesis opens later (the cold-start class, 12% of gold cells); the driver layer (D208).
docs/DECISIONS.md:2639:- Alex: "可以，但是不能因为有了这层我们的抽取就是非常的模版化缺少了hedge fund analyst 的灵魂"; on macro: "算是个global factor to all, 但影响正反面不一定". Measured before the decision (routing-analysis.md §11): with six analyst-seeded driver questions shown to the narrow placer, recall equals the old rule's (core 9/9/9), the sinks stay empty (6/1/5) and the neocloud, competitor-share and memory-cost statements land in their drivers (every landing read).
docs/DECISIONS.md:2641:- To build, in this order, each with the same gold and a one-week whole-path run: bootstrap seeding with dependencies, the judge's "drivers in force" block, re-placement of unplaced statements; then the macro themes with channels.
docs/DECISIONS.md:2650:  `unplaced` field, the `unplaced_statements` table and `store.add_unplaced` are removed; no re-placement mechanism is built. The
docs/DECISIONS.md:2688:  candidates or nothing, `folds_into` and `lost_if_folded` leave the schema. What the shown list did is owned elsewhere: the placement
docs/DECISIONS.md:2707:- Trace census of v38's 156 material losses: 94 have no corresponding question all week; 49 have the destination shown; 7 belong to an unshown candidate of their own item; 4 precede a later question; 1 fails the quote check and 1 disappears after matching rejects its candidate. The earlier claim that matching alone owns the remaining loss, or duplicate pages explain the placement misses, is withdrawn.
docs/DECISIONS.md:2708:- D190 remains a bounded next comparison, not a validated remedy for these losses. Its ACP pairs are directly affected; revenue/growth bypasses its same-measure gate and launch/shipment also conflicts at the identity check. A link-relabeling diagnostic reduces 17 pages to 13 and 178 links to 152 while retaining the same 144 records, restoring none of the drops; this is not a new model result. Any later improvement claim must report final core retention, meaning, placement and junk alongside page count, using the fixed reference. No paid call or production edit in this audit.
docs/DECISIONS.md:2713:- Before paid comparisons, the v38 preflight is itself defective: its old sift reports 77/841 statements kept, while the current production pre-placement sift keeps 831/841 over all 98 stored requests. One matching refusal also comes from applying a final ledger to a decision made before its own successor was written. The initial version-aware preflight repair failed an independent read-only review; the [review](research/2026-10-28-retention-audit/preflight-review-2026-10-28.txt) identifies source verification, exact shown-list boundaries, older output shapes and stage labels as missing dimensions. Rework and review the complete replay contract before implementation; do not treat the existing preflight PASS as proof of the current path.
docs/DECISIONS.md:2720:- The old scorer gives `kept_right` to two controls despite losing the metric “revenue”; quote overlap alone is not semantic correctness. The old `no_destination` category also was not implemented as specified. Trace, deterministic counterexample and source references: [evaluation and trace](research/2026-10-28-retention-audit/evaluation-and-trace-2026-10-28.md). A complete end-to-end result counts a fixed source fact only when its meaning and attribution reach the appropriate final question or, for distinct periods, the appropriate questions together. Report the local extraction, question availability, placement, matching and writing measures separately, including same-item candidates.
docs/DECISIONS.md:2721:- The 49 previously labelled misses have been traced to their archived requests and empty answers; the expected targets have not been independently established. One first lost the metric in extraction. Existing article 65 also loses the alternative's connection to Kyber in its standalone summary. No conclusion attributes all 49 to placement. The week also contains one missing placement answer out of 831 statements, counted by code as no home; it was labelled background. Production behaviour was not changed.
docs/DECISIONS.md:2723:- On 2026-10-29 an independently prompted model read the 49 archived cases without prior labels and produced a finding for each. Its tentative 5/21/23 split across placement, extraction and no suitable question is not an accepted census: it missed context carried by other statements in a real request and marked some destination choices uncertain while still assigning placement. The [case-by-case review](research/2026-10-28-retention-audit/independent-49-assessment-2026-10-29.md) keeps the raw model output and separates a confirmed missing revenue metric from disputed destinations. Model agreement is not a source, and model-authored judgements require calibration against the frozen standard.
docs/DECISIONS.md:2743:- The step numbers are those in the [steps 3–4 design](research/2026-10-27-stage34-gold/design.md): 1 read source into evidence and candidates; 2 read the historically correct question catalog and its full relevant evidence; 3 compare and record Jev's opinion; 4 decide where evidence belongs and how it changes the research argument. The current v38 pipeline has a distinct placement call and does not yet wire the D201 step-4 research-argument path; these are measured separately rather than counted as already built.
docs/DECISIONS.md:2772:- Six cases, fresh control and one replacement of the existing Action paragraph, Haiku three times each, same schema and source per pair; 36 calls within the existing $0.60 reservation cap. Four development cases and two explicitly source-known test cases; no full-pipeline run, product prompt edit, model promotion or rewritten old results. A failed comparison is recorded rather than answered by adding further prompt patches.
docs/DECISIONS.md:2814:Under D218's standing independent-iteration authorization and Alex's current Haiku-only request, the [scope repair](research/2026-10-29-claim-use/scope-repair/design.md) tests only a replacement purpose paragraph: information is relevant by its economic connection to the investment; forecasts and valuation scenarios can be useful without being established outcomes. Same structured schema, remaining prompt, sources, model and broad D226 rubric. Four known sources, fresh paired controls, three repeats,24 calls. No gold change, no hidden exact-label gate, no Luna, production integration or full-pipeline run. Prompt growth3603→3892 characters restores the omitted purpose rather than adding case-specific exceptions; token/cost changes are measured. All failed runs remain preserved. Original0.60-dollar planning cap unchanged.
docs/DECISIONS.md:2824:Alex directs that the thesis-library evidence standard and prior hedge-fund analyst ledger review must both be applied, allows reasonable ambiguity, and asks to stop and leave a complete retrospective and current state. Both worktrees’ `AGENTS.md` §8 now point to the sources and require judging source, investment use and question admission separately. The eight-question research review is context, not a replacement for Alex’s decisions, adopted PRDs or frozen gold. Existing routing rules, including D209, remain unchanged. Gold examples inform judgment; optional details or differing labels do not become a rigid pass/fail. The [handoff](research/2026-10-29-claim-use/handoff-2026-10-29.md) preserves the failures, evidence, experiment limitations, active worktree and next task. No further experiment, product change, default switch, commit, push or deployment.
docs/DECISIONS.md:3000:- Alex, after the end-to-end measurement and the reflection (`research/2026-10-31-reference-context/design-e2e.md`, `reflection-2026-10-31.md`: the placement call drops a third of the extracted core matters and 70% of the supporting ones for want of a question to file them under, while the questions those statements name — demand, inputs, competition and share, pricing, the company's own annual lines — are the root quantities and seven driver classes D208 designed and marked not built): the seed list for NVDA was put to him as a table (roots: FY2027 total revenue, data-center revenue, non-GAAP gross margin; drivers: hyperscaler capex 2026, server-memory contract price 2027, NVIDIA's share of 2026 data-center accelerator spending, the Rubin rack's price, Rubin shipping, China's H200 permission, AI Compute Partnership commitments). Alex: "可以吧".
docs/DECISIONS.md:3002:- Measured next (three draws against three control draws, the same 14 days, end to end): core and supporting matters reaching judgement and dropped for no home, noise reaching judgement, questions opened and their duplicates. The driver-in-force block for the judge and re-placement of earlier statements (D208's later steps) are not built here.
