ly, no rule text changed: the one-sentence reject list becomes a bulleted list the walk applies to each statement (name its kind, check the list, take it only when it has a kind and nothing on the list applies); 'Stop only at the end of the item' cut as a repeat; one clause of the signed direction ('most of an item is background'). The model had kept noise under a kind and applied the long reject sentence loosely. Version 36 (2026-10-29, arm on version 35, D244): entries identical to version 35; categories-v36 (arm A2): T8's reading block no longer asks for the author's ratings; an author's rating without a figure is an unargued verdict the role rejects (the model kept 'looks more like a hold' citing the T8 block). Version 35 (2026-10-29, arm on version 29, D244): entries identical to version 29; role-v35 (arm A1, page \u00a75.1 and D243 proposal 5): kind (3) keeps a named party's new claim; the reporter's framing or background, general risks or unargued verdicts, political or strategic views and typical claims that a firm leads or competes or that demand is strong or supply tight are one rejected class, common knowledge an analyst following the company already has, unless it gives a figure and a specific account. Version 29 (2026-10-29, direct read of the v28 answers): entries identical to version 28; role-v29 names the company's own leases beside its own borrowing as not an obligation; v28 opened a binding-obligation question on the company's own office lease after the guarantee wording named leases. Version 28 (2026-10-29, direct read of the v27 answers and the model's own account on the 8-K page): entries identical to version 27; role-v28 says whose obligation a guarantee or credit support covers (another party's debt, lease or revenue); v27 opened a binding-obligation question on an officer's standard indemnity agreement. Version 27 (2026-10-29, direct read of the v26 answers): entries identical to version 26; role-v27 counts one reported measure with its growt