lity/results.md 'Admission arm'): identical entries to version 20; role-v21 replaces the binding_obligation sentence: not yet signed -> a yes/no question due after the item within 18 months; already taken on, one deal or a programme -> a financing_amount question on the amount at the company's next annual filing, settled by its commitments note. Measured on the production bytes of the week's ACP articles: on the six that carry the obligation, control opened 0/18, the arm proposed 17/18 and the code kept 13/18. Version 20 (2026-10-28, routing-analysis.md \u00a76): identical entries and role to version 19; the version exists because from v20 the sift keeps a statement without a link and a separate placement call (placement.py, prompt placement-v1) decides the links to existing theses; v20 answers and handovers therefore differ in meaning from v19's. Version 19 (A, 2026-10-28, docs/research/2026-10-28-extraction-quality/results.md): identical entries and role to version 18; the version exists because from v19 the request's [Existing theses] block carries every open theme thesis beside the objects' own (code, extraction.THEMES_SHOWN_FROM / store.views_for_prompt(themes=True)) and the groups block prints only member ids the answer may link to, so v19 requests differ from v18 and the archive keeps them apart. Version 18 (D199, 2026-10-27 evening): the role is rewritten as the model reads it (evidence first; four kinds of material statement with examples; a walk over the whole page; a reject list with examples; links decided statement by statement; a rumour bears on a thesis as a confirmed statement does); T8's reading block asks for the author's forecasts, ratings, targets and cited figures, not general arguments. Measured arm by arm in docs/research/2026-10-27-single-call/log.md (B3\u2013B6). Other entries as v16. Version 16 (D199, 2026-10-27): identical entries to version 12; the version exists because role-v16 replaces the two contradicting gate rules (every statement is evidence by default / link only what a thesis directly concerns, omit the rest) with one decidable rule, and the request's closing line no longer invites an empty answer (extraction.EMPTY_LINE_FROM). The admission reasons stay v12's. Version 12 (D184, 2026-10-26): identical entries to version 11; the version exists because the extraction schema gains the admission fields (opens_as, folds_into, lost_if_folded, settled_by; code, extraction.admission_schema) and role-v12 states the four reasons a candidate may open. Version 10 (D167, 2026-10-25): identical to version 9; the version exists because the extraction schema's measure vocabulary gains market_size and project_cost (code, extraction.MEASURES_V10), so requests under v10 differ from v9 and the archive keeps them apart. 05-extraction.md: block 2 (what this category is and how to read it, from the classification rules) and block 4 (what to read out of it), same entries as categories-v6; version 9: declared groups carry aliases so code decides group identity and membership (D166); research groups only for ongoing matters, not for a company's own financial lines (D149/D164). Enum values come from the response schema.",
docs/research/2026-10-31-reference-context/codex-audit-role-v67-r1.log:1166:src/hivemind/prompts/categories-v65.json:2: "_note": "Version 65 (2026-10-31, arm on version 64, D250): entries identical to version 53; role-v65: role text identical to role-v53; review-v65.txt is review-v64.txt carrying standard version 5's four evidence boundaries (D250) on their rows: an arrangement only described as in place with no new step is background even with no date (item 1); a comparison the company, a partner or a third party publishes is a product detail (item 3); an analyst's reading of an event already recorded that adds no new fact or calculation is not kept (item 4); another company's matter is not kept when one cannot say through which path (demand, supply, competition, pricing and the like) it moves a question about the company, which covers D238's unrelated valuation, share price or deal (item 2). The header sends what a line does not cover to the check unless the line says it is kept: retold guidance and in-force forecasts and plans keep their place (5.3 retelling row) and a conditional valuation of the company is kept (5.3); a named analyst (5.3, D250 item 4); a partner's or customer's adoption goes to the check also beside a comparison. Examples from other industries (the standard's 415-watt card replaced). Read-only Codex rounds 1 and 2 (codex-review-v65-round*.md). Version 64 (2026-10-31, arm on version 63, D244): entries identical to version 53; role-v64: role text identical to role-v53; review-v64.txt is review-v63.txt written the way standard 5.3 is: the rows are not kept (5.3 不留, where v63 said 'usually fail'); each exception sits on the row it limits and says what that row does not cover, which the check then judges (5.3's boundary column: 不能用这一行删掉，按 5.1 判); the views row does not cover a conditional valuation (5.3) and the background row does not cover guidance or a forecast or plan still in force (5.3 retelling row); the closing keep list that overrode every row ('Keep these whenever they move such a question; none is dropped for the reasons above') is cut; the product row's launch exception names the product that carries the company's value (5.3 B row, 6) instead of v63's 'a product that sells or will sell at scale'; standard 5.1 and D240 are said once (fitting one of the four kinds does not keep an item; a missing amount, date or scale never drops one on its own); the political-stance row is added to carry the policy-step exception, as 5.3 does. The model's own account on 31 statements that both the gold and a blind reader reject named the closing keep list or one of its kinds as what kept them (loop log row 49); read-only Codex rounds 7 to 9. Version 63 (2026-10-31, arm on version 53, D244): entries identical to version 53; role-v63 (noise class, loop log row 46): role text identical to role-v53; review-v63.txt is review-v61.txt with the keep list narrowed where the full run showed it rescued noise: 'the company's own figure, guidance or decision' leaves the list (it rescued an officer's pay terms; kind 1 is still judged by the check and guidance stays protected in the opening line); a launch or shipment is of a product that sells or will sell at scale (standard 5.3 product row); a price change is the company's decision to change what its product costs (ruling 8), not one model's retail price. Version 53 (2026-10-30, arm on version 51, D244): entries identical to version 51; role-v53 (record-field class): the role text is role-v51's unchanged; the definitions of speaker, original_who and original_day (role-v52's sentence, split per field) travel in the schema as field descriptions (extraction.FIELD_NOTES, FIELD_NOTES_FROM = 53). Tests whether role-v52's rise in gold-rejected statements kept came from writing the definitions inside the role text that decides what to keep. Version 51 (2026-10-29, arm on version 42, D244): entries identical to version 42; main_driver's product branch written as the page's §3 B row (the