docs/research/2026-10-31-reference-context/codex-audit-role-v70-r1.log:163:- **Default configuration:** `poc/config/poc-v69.json` (D247): extraction role-v53 on `gpt-6-luna` (role-v51's text; `speaker`, `original_who` and `original_day` defined in the schema), the request showing no thesis and no group (D211); the placement call files each statement under the narrowest open question, and a statement no open question takes is dropped as `no home` (D207, D209); Jev matching with the collision judge (D190); judging with the theme block and the evidence in view (D195, D198). `scripts/replay.py`, the default-entry test and the README name it.
docs/research/2026-10-31-reference-context/codex-audit-role-v70-r1.log:171:1. Placement and drops (D207–D209): a separate placement call files statements; a statement no question takes is dropped with its reason and evaluation reads the drops.
docs/research/2026-10-31-reference-context/codex-audit-role-v70-r1.log:219:- D167–D169: no hard-coded identity; the measure vocabulary gains `market_size` and `project_cost`; the Jev engine (`views/jev_matching.py`, client `jev.py`) with the PRD's replacement definition, the shared succession rule and an answer for "the same quantity, another period"; a repeat may name the piece shown for the same evidence under another thesis.
docs/research/2026-10-31-reference-context/codex-audit-role-v70-r1.log:222:- D207–D211: extraction reads, then files (`extraction.read_item`, `extraction.file_reading`); under a ledger-blind version the request depends on the item alone, so the parallel day prepares the read early and files it at the item's turn; the placement call files statements, and a statement filed nowhere is dropped as `no home` (the `unplaced_statements` table is retired). After placement the sift's candidate rule runs again (`extraction.candidates_with_evidence`): a candidate left with none of its evidence is dropped, so no thesis opens without evidence (close-out review; 0 of 222 candidates under poc-v67, 25 of 5,805 over all stored loop answers).
docs/research/2026-10-31-reference-context/codex-audit-role-v70-r1.log:228:- The placement setting is checked before the paid extraction call; the credential guard in tests raises `pytest.fail`, which the pipeline's `except Exception` cannot swallow.
docs/research/2026-10-31-reference-context/codex-audit-role-v70-r1.log:238:**Evidence bloat, before anything else downstream:** not solved, reduced at the source. The window rule (D198, judging-v5) hides old pieces by recency, not by count: in the sealed three-month ledger the largest judging request after it (Data Center revenue) still showed 647 pieces (1,185 hidden), 93,634 input tokens, because a broad thesis took 40–60 new links a day. Placement under the one-home rule (D207–D209) cut the first week's links per item 3.3 → 1.82 and the largest thesis's links 106 → 52, the largest judging request 15,229 → 8,649 tokens (`english-v38-nvda-1w-2026-10-28` against the sealed ledger's same week), measured over one week with role-v22 only. The decisive test is the whole-pipeline run over the three-month window with `poc-v69` (on Alex's go, with a cap), read for links per thesis, the largest judging request and any halt; the structural answer, a versioned argument record per question for the judge to read, is designed nowhere yet (handoff plan T6).
docs/research/2026-10-31-reference-context/codex-audit-role-v70-r1.log:264:- Six cases, fresh control and one replacement of the existing Action paragraph, Haiku three times each, same schema and source per pair; 36 calls within the existing $0.60 reservation cap. Four development cases and two explicitly source-known test cases; no full-pipeline run, product prompt edit, model promotion or rewritten old results. A failed comparison is recorded rather than answered by adding further prompt patches.
docs/research/2026-10-31-reference-context/codex-audit-role-v70-r1.log:306:Under D218's standing independent-iteration authorization and Alex's current Haiku-only request, the [scope repair](research/2026-10-29-claim-use/scope-repair/design.md) tests only a replacement purpose paragraph: information is relevant by its economic connection to the investment; forecasts and valuation scenarios can be useful without being established outcomes. Same structured schema, remaining prompt, sources, model and broad D226 rubric. Four known sources, fresh paired controls, three repeats,24 calls. No gold change, no hidden exact-label gate, no Luna, production integration or full-pipeline run. Prompt growth3603→3892 characters restores the omitted purpose rather than adding case-specific exceptions; token/cost changes are measured. All failed runs remain preserved. Original0.60-dollar planning cap unchanged.
docs/research/2026-10-31-reference-context/codex-audit-role-v70-r1.log:316:Alex directs that the thesis-library evidence standard and prior hedge-fund analyst ledger review must both be applied, allows reasonable ambiguity, and asks to stop and leave a complete retrospective and current state. Both worktrees’ `AGENTS.md` §8 now point to the sources and require judging source, investment use and question admission separately. The eight-question research review is context, not a replacement for Alex’s decisions, adopted PRDs or frozen gold. Existing routing rules, including D209, remain unchanged. Gold examples inform judgment; optional details or differing labels do not become a rigid pass/fail. The [handoff](research/2026-10-29-claim-use/handoff-2026-10-29.md) preserves the failures, evidence, experiment limitations, active worktree and next task. No further experiment, product change, default switch, commit, push or deployment.
