docs/research/2026-10-31-reference-context/codex-audit-placement-v2-r1.log:52:- **Default configuration:** `poc/config/poc-v69.json` (D247): extraction role-v53 on `gpt-6-luna` (role-v51's text; `speaker`, `original_who` and `original_day` defined in the schema), the request showing no thesis and no group (D211); the placement call files each statement under the narrowest open question, and a statement no open question takes is dropped as `no home` (D207, D209); Jev matching with the collision judge (D190); judging with the theme block and the evidence in view (D195, D198). `scripts/replay.py`, the default-entry test and the README name it.
docs/research/2026-10-31-reference-context/codex-audit-placement-v2-r1.log:60:1. Placement and drops (D207–D209): a separate placement call files statements; a statement no question takes is dropped with its reason and evaluation reads the drops.
docs/research/2026-10-31-reference-context/codex-audit-placement-v2-r1.log:108:- D167–D169: no hard-coded identity; the measure vocabulary gains `market_size` and `project_cost`; the Jev engine (`views/jev_matching.py`, client `jev.py`) with the PRD's replacement definition, the shared succession rule and an answer for "the same quantity, another period"; a repeat may name the piece shown for the same evidence under another thesis.
docs/research/2026-10-31-reference-context/codex-audit-placement-v2-r1.log:111:- D207–D211: extraction reads, then files (`extraction.read_item`, `extraction.file_reading`); under a ledger-blind version the request depends on the item alone, so the parallel day prepares the read early and files it at the item's turn; the placement call files statements, and a statement filed nowhere is dropped as `no home` (the `unplaced_statements` table is retired). After placement the sift's candidate rule runs again (`extraction.candidates_with_evidence`): a candidate left with none of its evidence is dropped, so no thesis opens without evidence (close-out review; 0 of 222 candidates under poc-v67, 25 of 5,805 over all stored loop answers).
docs/research/2026-10-31-reference-context/codex-audit-placement-v2-r1.log:117:- The placement setting is checked before the paid extraction call; the credential guard in tests raises `pytest.fail`, which the pipeline's `except Exception` cannot swallow.
docs/research/2026-10-31-reference-context/codex-audit-placement-v2-r1.log:127:**Evidence bloat, before anything else downstream:** not solved, reduced at the source. The window rule (D198, judging-v5) hides old pieces by recency, not by count: in the sealed three-month ledger the largest judging request after it (Data Center revenue) still showed 647 pieces (1,185 hidden), 93,634 input tokens, because a broad thesis took 40–60 new links a day. Placement under the one-home rule (D207–D209) cut the first week's links per item 3.3 → 1.82 and the largest thesis's links 106 → 52, the largest judging request 15,229 → 8,649 tokens (`english-v38-nvda-1w-2026-10-28` against the sealed ledger's same week), measured over one week with role-v22 only. The decisive test is the whole-pipeline run over the three-month window with `poc-v69` (on Alex's go, with a cap), read for links per thesis, the largest judging request and any halt; the structural answer, a versioned argument record per question for the judge to read, is designed nowhere yet (handoff plan T6).
