docs/research/2026-10-31-reference-context/codex-audit-role-v67-r3.log:491:2595-- Alex, on the arm1 result and the proposal: "你接着做，需要非常严谨的看结果和测量". Census first ([labels](research/2026-10-27-stage34-gold/replacements-47-labels.json), every pair read): of the run's 47 retirements, 22 are the owner's later value or status of the same claim (right under rule E), 20 retired a statement that should have stayed (10 a contradiction or qualification, among them a denial erasing the delay report, "subject to final agreements" erasing the $500bn announcement; 10 a different matter), 5 were restatements mislabelled. Jev's `supersedes` label does not separate them: 17 of 22 right and 12 of 20 wrong carry it; with "confirms or denies" split out (`jev_contradicts.py`) 4 wrong ones flip to `contradicts` but so do 3 right ones. No label the matcher gives is safe to retire on.
docs/research/2026-10-31-reference-context/codex-audit-role-v67-r3.log:492:2596-- Decided: `writing` no longer calls `store.replace`. A `replace` decision stores the incoming piece, links it wherever the target is linked, and records the pair in a new `revisions` table (old, new, said day, seq); both pieces stay in force. `replacement_refused` becomes `revision_refused` with the same conditions (a stated day, a tier at least the old piece's, the same party for views and rumours): refused means stored as new without the relation, as before. The late-older-statement rule is unchanged. `replacements` is history: read by every present reader as before, never written again. `store.evidence_in_force` carries `revises` (the predecessor by revision) and judging prints "It revises eX (both in force)" so the judge sees the path; the library UI and service do not show revisions yet (open). The Jev criteria are unchanged: the split was measured and not adopted (3 false `contradicts` on right revisions against 4 catches).
docs/research/2026-10-31-reference-context/codex-audit-role-v67-r3.log:495:2599-- Regression week ([results](research/2026-10-27-stage34-gold/results.md), `english-v34b-nvda-week-2026-10-27`, $0.23, 98 items, none failed): the whole path runs with the revision rule; `replacements` gains no row. Counts differ from the v18 week (129 against 176 evidence rows, 12 against 9 theses) because extraction is a sampler, not because of the writer; the writer's effect is proved on the decisions themselves. Reading the week's one `replace` decision found a second silent loss in the same code path: an incoming statement said before its target was logged in `late_statements` and linked nowhere (both weeks dropped SemiAnalysis's Kyber delay report this way; the three-month run dropped the SharonAI backstop figure; 1 of 3,216 decisions, each a material statement). Fixed in the same slice: an older statement is stored and linked as one more piece, no revision recorded, the log row kept. Test red on the old writer, green after; suite 209. Observed, not fixed here: 34 of 1,530 stored pieces carry a non-ISO `original_day` ("2026-07-05 to 2026-07-06", "2026-03"), which is what made the Kyber report "older"; an extraction-contract item for the next pass.
