docs/research/2026-10-31-reference-context/codex-audit-role-v69-r1.log:1874:3. **The company-wide quantity sentence is a new rule, not D207’s one-home rule.** The draft says such a question “is moved **only by a figure or guidance for that quantity, or by a named customer’s order, plan or cut with a size**.” [D207](/Users/lchingen/hivemind-extraction-quality-2026-10-28/docs/DECISIONS.md:2630) is a *placement* rule: company-wide figure questions take “their own figures, guidance **and management statements**,” and it files a statement under the narrowest question. It does not say that other evidence cannot change the likely answer, and it does not impose the draft’s customer-size test. Section 5.1 asks whether the statement makes an answer more or less likely; D240 rejects a missing-size gate.
